System 573: bring the R3000 fetch PC out of the PSX core (PC-sampling profiler).

Run C (2026-09-17, ddrextrm) showed the game rendering exactly 30 frames a second
whenever a background video is decoding and exactly 60 otherwise, with every
occupancy counter (MDEC, GPU, DMA-paused, CPU memory-stall) well below saturation.
Occupancy levels cannot tell a spin-wait from real work, so they could not say
WHERE the CPU's 33 ms go. A PC-sampling profile can: rtl/s573_prof_pc.v samples
this tap every 1024 clk1x into a 256-bin histogram (4 KB bins over the game's
executable, which loads at 0x80010000) and the HPS dumps it once a second, to be
read against the disassembly (docs/2026-09-18-ddrextrm-video-path-from-sources.md).

cpu.vhd  : new output dbg573_pc = the fetch PC register, a concurrent assignment.
psx_top / psx_mister : pass-through. Observation only -- no existing signal changes.
Stacks on 0029 (frame profile taps) and 0030 (MDEC timing switch).

--- a/rtl/cpu.vhd
+++ b/rtl/cpu.vhd
@@ -81,7 +81,10 @@
       cpu_export            : out cpu_export_type := ((others => (others => '0')), (others => '0'), (others => '0'), (others => '0'));
 -- synthesis translate_on
       
-      debug_firstGTE        : in  std_logic
+      debug_firstGTE        : in  std_logic;
+      -- System 573 (psx_patches 0031): the fetch PC, brought out for the PC-sampling
+      -- profiler (rtl/s573_prof_pc.v). Observation only; nothing reads it back.
+      dbg573_pc             : out std_logic_vector(31 downto 0) := (others => '0')
    );
 end entity;
 
@@ -479,6 +482,9 @@
    
 begin 
 
+   -- System 573 (psx_patches 0031): fetch-PC tap for the PC-sampling profiler.
+   dbg573_pc <= std_logic_vector(PC);
+
    -- IO
    mem_request       <= mem1_request or mem1_request_latched or mem4_request when (memoryMuxBusy = '0' or mem_done = '1') else '0';
    mem_isCache       <= FetchLastCache     when (mem1_request_latched = '1') else mem1_cacherequest;
